<title>UNITED NATIONS: Iraq-UN oil deal dickering begins post-US election.</title>
<headline>Iraq-UN oil deal dickering begins post-US election.</headline>
<byline>Patrick Connole</byline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>With the U.S. presidential election out of the way, the cat-and-mouse game over Iraq's oil-for-food deal with the United Nations has begun again in earnest.</p>
<p>For most of this year, the U.S. election has hovered over the U.N. &quot;oil for food&quot; deal, acting as the marker for when diplomats reckoned the scheme might actually stand a chance of implementation.</p>
</text>
